WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:10.500
"Soul Food That’s
Good for the Soul"

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.400
The burden of cardiovascular disease
in the African American community

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.000
remains high and is a primary
cause of disparities

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.560
in life expectancy between
African Americans and whites.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.840
Why is there such
an excess burden?

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.520
Because of an excess burden
of risk factors, for example,

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.480
high blood pressure, diabetes,
obesity, and high cholesterol.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.120
And what’s underlying
those risk factors?

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.880
Much can be traced
back to diet.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:41.880
Among the ethnic groups,
the proportions of people

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.740
meeting healthy diet
recommendations

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.620
were generally lowest
among Blacks.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.980
In this national survey,
most Black Americans

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.100
were found to be eating
a particularly poor diet,

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.574
as defined by
the American Heart Association.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.640
African Americans
may face unique challenges

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:01.620
to adherence to dietary
recommendations,

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.320
and one such challenge
is an alignment

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.380
with a cultural tradition
of “soul food.”

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:11.220
Now some soul food components
are fantastic.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:15.180
You can’t get much healthier than
collard greens and sweet potatoes,

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:20.220
tomatoes, legumes (dried peas
and beans like black-eyed peas),

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.140
watermelon, blackberries,
corn, and okra.

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.360
It’s all making me hungry.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.974
But conversely, soul food
can also be high

00:01:27.974 --> 00:01:31.140
in added fats, sugars,
and salt, with prominent use

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.860
of high-fat meats not to mention
the use of deep frying.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:37.500
So, like fried
chicken and chitlins,

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.658
which are pig intestines,

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.940
foods that can be high
in sodium and saturated fat—

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:45.591
dietary factors linked
to chronic disease.

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:50.154
Where did the pig intestines
custom come from?

00:01:50.154 --> 00:01:52.080
You have to trace the roots.

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:55.800
Soul food is what the enslaved
Africans were forced

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:59.605
to come up with in the Deep South
to survive during slavery.

00:01:59.605 --> 00:02:03.300
That’s in stark contrast
to traditional West African diets

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:06.420
where they come from, which
were predominantly plant-based,

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:09.960
centered on a foundation
of greens and fruits and legumes

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:13.380
and nuts and vegetables, and whole
grains, and even more vegetables.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:16.620
However, these traditions
have been westernized,

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:19.380
bastardized into a diet
high in fried foods,

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:23.204
sweetened beverages,
and red and processed meats.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:26.940
But the good news is more
and more African Americans

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:30.420
are adopting plant-based diets
to combat their health problems,

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:34.860
helped by a growing movement
of vegan soul food restaurants

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:37.740
that serve healthier,
plant-based meals.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:41.280
Soul food scholar Adrian Miller
even wrote that after eating

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.320
his way across the country,
it was clear to him

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:47.460
that soul food’s creative energy
burns brightest in restaurants

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:51.840
that are targeting upscale,
vegetarian, or vegan clientele.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:54.540
Are they reaching the people
who need it most, though?

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.460
Well, they do
tend to be located

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.760
in higher African American,
higher poverty areas.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.220
A signiﬁcant number
of restaurants were classiﬁed

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:06.240
in food desert zones, where
there’s a dearth of supermarkets,

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.360
implying their potential
to provide healthier meals

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:11.340
to residents in the
surrounding neighborhoods.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:14.460
Therefore, having more
vegan soul food restaurants

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.340
and growing movements
centered on Black veganism,

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:21.300
may provide opportunities
to inﬂuence the nutrition habits

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.000
in the African American community,
especially since some

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.880
are even able to offer
cooking classes.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:29.580
So, establishing public
health partnerships

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.920
with vegan soul food
restaurants to get more

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:33.829
African American adults
to eat plant-based foods

00:03:33.829 --> 00:03:36.720
could be a promising
first step in reducing

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.300
some of the Black/white
health disparities.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:43.140
“We’re not meat
shamers,” said owners

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:44.460
of vegan soul
food restaurants

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:46.740
promoting healthy eating in the
African American community.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:52.080
“We’re plant pushers,” trying
to tie the best of soul food’s origins

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:56.280
to a fourteenth century
plant-centric West African diet,

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:59.580
in hopes of making people feel
that being vegan is in fact

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:03.480
a legitimate part of Black
culture and Black identity.

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:07.140
Even potentially tying
into the concept of social justice,

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:10.500
in an attempt to reverse the eﬀects
of targeted marketing eﬀorts

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:14.500
by fast food companies to children
in communities of color.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:16.200
This movement has been helped

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:18.660
by a plant-positive
who's who of Black culture,

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.040
not just luminaries like

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.960
like Coretta Scott King
and Cory Booker,

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:26.340
but the likes of NBA stars,
Samuel L. Jackson, and Beyoncé,

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:31.069
and influentially the late
activist Dick Gregory,

00:04:31.069 --> 00:04:33.720
known in popular
culture as a comedian,

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:36.900
but was also an outspoken
vegan health advocate

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:40.800
influenced by Alvenia Fulton
who imagined soul food

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:43.320
that was actually
good for the soul.

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:46.620
Instead of celebrating
the fact that slaveholders

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:49.159
denied enslaved people
access to quality foods,

00:04:49.159 --> 00:04:51.000
she persuaded
Black communities

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:54.420
to view food as an agent
of health and healing,

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:56.460
advocating fresh,
whole foods as the path

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.500
to alleviating or reversing

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:01.763
the crippling burden
of chronic disease.

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:05.460
Black vegetarians and vegans
are showing a plant-based diet

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:08.340
isn’t just for white people—
and never was.

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:13.860
In fact, you can go back centuries
to The Liberator back in the 1800s,

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:17.520
the abolitionist publication
where William Lloyd Garrison

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:20.580
wrote in his famous essay:
"I will be as harsh as truth,

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:23.595
and as uncompromising as justice."

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:27.991
Well, in an 1853 issue,
it was written that:

00:05:27.991 --> 00:05:31.620
“A man whose stomach is crammed
with animal abominations…

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:34.680
can no more appreciate lofty moral
and intellectual teachings,

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:37.740
than a swine can appreciate
pearl necklaces.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:41.520
Logic, humor, and eloquence
are wasted on such persons.”

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.280
"If only the American people
took more thought

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:47.340
what they should eat
and drink, obeying the rules

00:05:47.340 --> 00:05:49.620
impressed upon them
by experience and science,"

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:51.480
(by which they meant
a vegetarian diet),

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:55.680
(America) "would be half-converted
to Anti-Slavery, Peace,

00:05:55.680 --> 00:06:01.326
Temperance, Land Reform,
Woman’s Rights, etc., in a single year."

